From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:29:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Wait for a package lock without stopping the other jobs

The fetch and the install of packages run as coroutines of one process,
and a package lock taken by another process was waited for with a
blocking flock. The wait stopped every coroutine of the process,
including the ones that held other package locks, so two processes that
each held one lock and wanted the other's stopped forever at no CPU.

Two configures of different projects show it: one holds lka while it
installs it and wants lkb; the other holds lkb while it fetches it and
wants lka. Both stay asleep until they are killed.

Inside a coroutine the lock is now tried again every 100 ms, and the
wait yields to the scheduler, so the holder finishes and lets go. Outside
a coroutine the blocking lock stays.

Changes-build-output: no

---
 xmake/core/package/package.lua | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xmake/core/package/package.lua b/xmake/core/package/package.lua
index ec7b874..eee2972 100644
--- a/xmake/core/package/package.lua
+++ b/xmake/core/package/package.lua
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@ local language       = require("language/language")
 local language_menu  = require("language/menu")
 local sandbox        = require("sandbox/sandbox")
 local sandbox_os     = require("sandbox/modules/os")
+local scheduler      = require("base/scheduler")
 local sandbox_module = require("sandbox/modules/import/core/sandbox/module")
 
 -- new an instance
@@ -840,10 +841,17 @@ function _instance:lock(opt)
     else
         utils.cprint("${color.warning}package(%s) is being accessed by other processes, please wait!", self:name())
     end
-    local ok, errors = self:filelock():lock(opt)
-    if not ok then
-        os.raise(errors)
+    if not scheduler:co_running() then
+        local ok, errors = self:filelock():lock(opt)
+        if not ok then
+            os.raise(errors)
+        end
+        return true
     end
+    while not self:filelock():trylock(opt) do
+        sandbox_os.sleep(100)
+    end
+    return true
 end
 
 -- unlock the whole package
